"Intoxicate", while technically correct, gives a rather the wrong impressio=
n.=A0 Generally, intoxication is thought of as a relatively pleasant experi=
ence, a high, not (except, perhaps, in the very long run) a dangerous one.=
=A0 {vindu} is pretty clearly meant to refer to something dangerous in the =
short run and thoroughly unpleasant, hence both "poison" and "venomous" and=
, indeed, "toxic" -- yew leaves, say.=A0=A0 I'd stick with "poison" in the =
English.




